Folks:
=20
I think I've cracked it - basically by guessing which buttons they were lik=
ely to use for reset - I knew the two required for E2 reset so I thought th=
at three wouldn't be beyond them for the E3.
=20
1. Remove power cord from E3
2. Hold down: DELETE=2C STOP and HANDSFREE together
3. Keep holding all three and insert power cord
4. Keep holding all three - E3 boots as normal but after about 15/20 second=
s displays message "Initialising system" (I can't remember the exact wordin=
g)
5. Keep holding until you have your final screen which prompts you to regis=
ter as a new user (you may let go now)
6. Old address book entries and other previously stored information is gone=
.=20
7. Have a cup of tea.
=20
Best regards
=20
James


